 },
 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:09:26.637730Z",
 "text": "Yes, this clause is enforceable. \n\nUnder section 4 of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a lease provision is void only if it is inconsistent with the Act. Section 26(1)(a) explicitly permits a landlord to enter a rental unit at any time without written notice in cases of emergency. Because a fire, flood, or burst pipe constitutes a genuine emergency, this lease clause simply restates the landlord's lawful statutory right of entry and does not conflict with the Act.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 26",
